From: Yoonji Park <koreapyj@dcmys.kr>
Subject: ASoC: qdsp6: q6voice: selectable AFE ports, topology, CS-call attach
 and VoLTE path

Replace the hardcoded MI2S ports with a struct q6voice_path_cfg: raw AFE
port ids (so the RT proxy ports 0x2000/0x2001 can be used), vocproc
topologies (default or VSS_IVOCPROC_TOPOLOGY_ID_NONE), attach mode
(MVM attach, CVS passive session + CVS attach, or both) and optional
START_VOICE. q6voice_start_path()/q6voice_stop_path() start the path
explicitly and undo every step on failure so a start can be retried.
Add q6cvs passive session/attach commands, a per-command trace hook
(q6voice_set_trace) reporting handle and DSP status, zero-initialise the
command structs (stack garbage was sent in session names).

Add Q6VOICE_PATH_VOLTE (path/session index 2, same as the downstream
msm-4.x q6voice VOC_PATH_VOLTE_PASSIVE) and let q6mvm/q6cvs join the
CVD session "default volte voice" created by the modem's IMS audio, the
same way "default modem voice" is joined for CS calls (downstream
q6voice.c uses that string for both MVM and CVS passive sessions when
is_volte_session()).

Signed-off-by: Yoonji Park <koreapyj@dcmys.kr>
